{
  "phase": "2",
  "description": "Enhanced messaging infrastructure with Boolean, BlockContext, and SmallInteger",
  "comments": [
    "IMPORTANT: Array must be created FIRST before any other classes that have instance variables.",
    "This is because the instance variable lists are stored as Array objects, and need the Array",
    "class to exist when they are created. Otherwise they will have no class pointer.",
    "",
    "IMPORTANT: String must be created BEFORE Symbol since Symbol inherits from String.",
    "If Symbol is processed first, it won't be able to set String as its superclass.",
    "",
    "This enhanced version includes:",
    "- Boolean/True/False for conditional logic",
    "- BlockContext for closures and control flow", 
    "- SmallInteger for arithmetic",
    "- Proper Blue Book header encoding (primitive | (largeContext << 9) | (tempCount << 10))"
  ],
